; a structure that holds things inside it. defines an enclosed volume.
; the container is the kshetra: the bounded field that holds its contents.
; what a container does:
; holds liquids: cup, bottle, tank, pot — liquid fills to surface level
; holds gases: sealed vessel — gas pressure acts on all walls
; holds solids: box, bag, bin — things rest inside
; 
; container in thermodynamics: the ideal gas law assumes a sealed container.
; PV = nRT: P is pressure on walls. V is container volume.
; heating a sealed container of gas: pressure rises (V constant, T rises → P rises).
; a pot of water: open container. water heated → temperature rises → boils → steam escapes.
; 
; pressure vessel: a container designed to hold pressurised gas or liquid.
; failure: if internal pressure > material strength → explosion (rapid release).
; 
; in 3d: a container is a concave mesh — interior visible, exterior is structure.

(kosha container
  (vishesa structures-varga common-sense-varga)
  (swarupa enclosure)
  (yukta volume liquid gas solid pressure temperature normal-force domain-3d))
